# coordination.conf — this repo's autonomy + cross-repo-comms configuration.
#
# `wai-init` writes this into `docs/architecture/coordination.conf` (proposal-only) and refines
# it on each re-run. `coordination-lint.sh` validates it; a red lint STOPS setup.
#
# Format: KEY="value". PARSED, NEVER SOURCED. A repo-local file a script EXECUTES is an injection
# vector, and the tools that read this run on a machine with git credentials and a webhook secret in
# the environment. Nothing here is ever `. sourced` — every consumer greps the one key it needs.
#
# THIS FILE IS CONTRACT-DOMAIN. It decides what an agent may do WITHOUT a human. An agent-merged edit
# to it could arm autonomy or widen its blast radius with no human in the loop — so it is off-limits
# to the tuning pass, it is protected by the merge gate's guardrail floor, and it is fail-closed:
# every default below is the SAFE state (autonomy off, comms none). An ABSENT file means exactly the
# same thing as this file's defaults — autonomy is off. You opt IN, explicitly, or you get nothing.

# ── AUTONOMY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off by default, and off is a real answer, not a placeholder. Set to "yes" ONLY after the four
# preconditions below are met — coordination-lint enforces them, and refuses to let autonomy arm
# without them:
#   1. AUTONOMY_SAFE_PATHS is non-empty          (the ALLOWLIST — an agent may drain a PR only if
#                                                  EVERY path it touches is inside this set)
#   2. CONTRACT_PATHS is non-empty in merge-gate.conf   (the blocklist floor is actually defined)
#   3. ERASURE_PATHS is non-empty in merge-gate.conf    (the GDPR-erasure surface is actually named)
#   4. AUTONOMY_AFFIRMED is present               (a human affirmed THIS surface, on a date, by hash)
AUTONOMY_ENABLED="no"

# The six policy domains that stay the human's IN EVERY MODE. This is the FLOOR: a human may only
# WIDEN it (add tokens), never narrow it. coordination-lint sources the authoritative floor from
# `excluded-domains.sh --list-domains --policy-only` and fails if any of the six is missing here.
#
# Each entry is three colon-separated fields:  TAG:human-name:catalog-id
#   TAG          — the canonical domain-family tag from `agent-git-protocol.md § Excluded domains`.
#                  This is the suite-wide, non-numeric vocabulary the whole autonomy model keys on —
#                  it is NOT a catalog ID and does not rebind across repos.
#   human-name   — the domain in words, so the file reads without a decoder ring.
#   catalog-id   — an OPTIONAL slot, EMPTY in this template on purpose. A bare catalog ID copied into
#                  a template rebinds to a different meaning in every repo (ADR-0003), so the template
#                  ships none. If you want an ID anchor, `wai-init` RESOLVES the human-name
#                  against THIS repo's quality-attributes.md at write time and fills it here; a filled
#                  ID that no longer resolves is caught by coordination-lint's dangling-anchor check.
AUTONOMY_EXCLUDED="EX-PAY:payment-token-billing: EX-AUTH:auth-login-and-user-management: EX-API:api-contract: EX-SEC:security: EX-MIG:destructive-migration: EX-GDPR:gdpr-erasure:"

# The ALLOWLIST that actually authorises autonomy. Autonomy eligibility is NOT "the blocklist did not
# trip" — a blocklist is under-inclusive by construction (it cannot know a novel risky path). It is
# "every touched path is provably inside a human-affirmed safe set". Space-separated globs, same
# syntax as merge-gate.conf. EMPTY (the default) means NO path is safe ⇒ autonomy drains nothing.
AUTONOMY_SAFE_PATHS=""

# The human affirmation. A date + a short hash/fingerprint of the safe set the human signed off on,
# e.g. AUTONOMY_AFFIRMED="2026-08-02 sha256:1a2b3c…". EMPTY ⇒ unaffirmed ⇒ autonomy stays off, no
# matter what the paths say. This is the "a human looked at THIS blast radius and said yes" record.
AUTONOMY_AFFIRMED=""

# Risk PATHS are NOT duplicated here. CONTRACT_PATHS, MIGRATION_PATHS and ERASURE_PATHS live in
# `merge-gate.conf` and are INHERITED — one source of truth for "which paths are dangerous", read by
# both the merge gate and the autonomy classifier. Editing them in one place changes both, on purpose.

# ── CROSS-REPO COMMS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How agents in DIFFERENT repos signal each other. The default — "none" — is the file-based handoff
# (each repo's gitignored temp/ mailbox, human-triggered), which needs no secret and no network.
#
# Allowed COMMS_TOOL values (a fixed set coordination-lint checks against):
#   none                — file-based temp/ handoff (the safe default; also the degrade target when a
#                         configured tool is unreachable or the forge is not GitHub)
#   github-coordination — a shared GitHub issue/label as the wake-signal
#   slack | discord | matrix — third-party notify transports (a channel + a webhook, NOTHING more:
#                         the tool only NOTIFIES; the sensitive spec stays in-repo, never on the wire)
COMMS_TOOL="none"

# The channel/room identifier the wake-signal is posted to (e.g. "#eng-agents", a channel ID, a room
# alias). An IDENTIFIER, not a secret. Empty when COMMS_TOOL=none.
COMMS_CHANNEL=""

# *** SECRET HYGIENE — STORE THE ENV-VAR *NAME*, NEVER THE SECRET ITSELF. ***
# This value is the NAME of an environment variable that holds the webhook URL/token at runtime —
# for example  COMMS_WEBHOOK_ENV="TEAM_COORD_WEBHOOK_URL"  — and the process reads
# `$TEAM_COORD_WEBHOOK_URL` when it needs to post. It is NOT the URL, NOT the token, NOT `https://…`.
# A literal secret committed here is a leaked secret in git history forever; coordination-lint
# HARD-FAILS on any value that looks like a URL or a known token shape. Must match ^[A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*$.
COMMS_WEBHOOK_ENV=""

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# EXAMPLE — a team repo that has opted into a bounded autonomous drain over its docs and tests only,
# and posts a wake-signal to Slack. THIS IS NOT A DEFAULT. Delete it; do not uncomment it verbatim.
#
# AUTONOMY_ENABLED="yes"
# The active key stays on ONE line — it is parsed single-line, so a "\"-continued value would be
# silently truncated to its first line. The seventh entry WIDENS the floor with a repo-local domain
# (allowed; narrowing is not):
# AUTONOMY_EXCLUDED="EX-PAY:payment-token-billing: EX-AUTH:auth-login-and-user-management: EX-API:api-contract: EX-SEC:security: EX-MIG:destructive-migration: EX-GDPR:gdpr-erasure: EX-RELEASE:release-status-doc:docs/RELEASE.md"
# AUTONOMY_SAFE_PATHS="docs/** tests/** *.md"
# AUTONOMY_AFFIRMED="2026-08-02 sha256:1a2b3c4d"
# COMMS_TOOL="slack"
# COMMS_CHANNEL="#eng-agents"
# COMMS_WEBHOOK_ENV="TEAM_COORD_WEBHOOK_URL"
